# Fix / update desktop (Windows runtime)

When the user says they need to **fix, update, debug, or change the desktop app** (also: Windows app, Tauri, WebView2, native shell, Python sidecar on desktop):

1. **Read first:** [`docs/PWA_DESKTOP_COMPAT.md`](../../docs/PWA_DESKTOP_COMPAT.md)
2. **Follow skill:** `.cursor/skills/fix-desktop/SKILL.md`

## Meaning of this intent

- Target runtime is the **private Windows 11 Tauri app**
- If the bug is **desktop-only**, fix in `src-tauri/` or `js/platform/windows/` first
- If shared code must change, use a **platform adapter** — keep the PWA path working
- **Do not** rewrite shared map/dual-screen/widget logic to be Tauri-shaped for everyone

## Allowed focus

- `src-tauri/`, `desktop/sidecar/`, `js/platform/windows/`
- Thin adapters in shared modules that branch via `js/platform` contracts (web provider unchanged)
- Desktop-only widgets via `requiredCapabilities` in `js/widgets/registry.js`

## Forbidden for this intent

- `@tauri-apps/*` imports outside `js/platform/windows/`
- Copying widgets into a Windows-only folder tree
- Changing PWA service-worker / install behavior as a desktop fix
- Breaking `window.open` (or other browser) dual-screen path while adding Tauri windows

## Verify before done

- `npm test`
- `npm run build` or `npm run build:web` (**PWA must still build**)
- `npm run build:desktop`
- Desktop smoke for the bug; **browser smoke too** if any shared file changed
